  // The Mac app's symbols: each the outline of the SF Symbol the app draws, traced at 24 points in the weight the app mostly draws it in, or the weight after its name's colon, which `weight` names. `frames` holds, at each size the boards draw the symbol at, the width and height SwiftUI lays it out in, then how far right and down of that frame's centre the symbol sits, all in points, as a window at 2 pixels a point lays it out and draws it. SwiftUI rounds each frame to a half point in steps that no scaling of the symbol at 24 gives: exclamationmark.circle in semibold is 19 points square at 15.47, where its frame at 24 scales to 18.47. SwiftUI also draws the symbol off the frame's centre, by as much as 0.55 points and by amounts no scaling gives either: pause.fill in bold sits 0.13 left of and 0.11 below the centre of its frame at 10 points. `ink` is the left, top, right and bottom of what it draws, in points at 24 around the frame's centre (12, 12), before SwiftUI moves the symbol off it.
